/** \page cp-submodules Submodules

Due to Marmalade being a C++ project, some libraries are required to be compiled alongside the engine.

These are managed by the submodules system.

Submodules are effectively git repositories cloned to a local directory, typically`vendor/`.

<b>TL;DR: `python submodules.py restore` to download all submodules</b>

\section submodules-script Submodules Script

The `submodules.py` Python script in the project root is the main method of managing submodules.

Submodules can be added with the `add` command:

```bash
python submodules.py add https://github.com/path/to/repo vendor/library
```

Note, when adding a submodule, the directory should also be added to .gitignore.

Similarly, submodules can be deleted with the `delete` command:

```bash
python submodules.py delete vendor/library
```

When cloning the Marmalade repo, the `restore` command can be used to download and patch all submodules:

```bash
python submodules.py restore
```

\section submodules-json submodules.json

The submodules.json file is the source of truth for all submodules. It contains a single `submodules` array.

Each submodule contains the following properties:

<table>
<tr>
<th>Property</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`path`</td>
<td>The local path of the submodule</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`url`</td>
<td>The remote Git URL of the submodule. Recommend to use HTTPS as opposed to SSH</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`branch`</td>
<td>The branch to fetch from the remote repository</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`commit`</td>
<td>The SHA1 hash of the specific commit to fetch from the remote repository</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`patches`</td>
<td>An array of patches to apply. See \ref patching section below.</td>
</tr>
</table>

\section patching Patching

The submodules system allows patches to be applied to submodules. Patch files can be specified by adding them to the `patches` array in the `submodules.json` file.

Patches can be created by modifying the submodules code, then executing the `git diff > mypatch.patch` command. This automatically generates a patch file from the uncommitted changes.

\section submodules-lock submodules.lock

The `submodules.lock` file is generated automatically on restore, and contains the commit hashes and branches of each submodule.

*/
